Kingpin: Life of Crime game library — licensing
===============================================

This repository contains code from four sources with different owners and
different terms. Read this before copying, redistributing, or shipping anything
built from it.

Nothing in this repository grants you rights to Xatrix's or Interplay's code.
The repository owner has no authority to grant them and does not purport to.
Only section 4 is an actual licence grant, and it covers a small part of the
tree: the repository owner's own contributions, not the SDK code they were made
to.


1. The Kingpin SDK — Xatrix Entertainment / Interplay Productions
-----------------------------------------------------------------

Copyright (c) 1999 Xatrix Entertainment, Inc. and Interplay Productions.
All rights reserved.

Almost everything in src/ originates in the Kingpin: Life of Crime game-source
SDK, released by Xatrix in September 1999 as kpsdk.zip. That archive shipped one
terms document, sdk/readme.txt, which is the retail game's end-user licence with
a single phrase changed ("This copy of Kingpin: Life of Crime" became "This SDK
for Kingpin: Life of Crime"). Its operative clause reads, verbatim:

    This SDK for Kingpin: Life of Crime (the "Software") is intended solely for
    your personal noncommercial home entertainment use. You may not decompile,
    reverse engineer, or disassemble the Software, except as permitted by law.
    Interplay Productions, Xatrix, and Id Software retain[s] all right, title
    and interest in the Software including all intellectual property rights
    embodied therein and derivatives thereof.  The Software, including, without
    limitation, all code, data structures, characters, images, sounds, text,
    screens, game play, derivative works and all other elements of the Software
    may not be copied, resold, rented, leased, distributed (electronically or
    otherwise), used on pay-per-play, coin-op or other for-charge basis, or for
    any commercial purpose. Any permissions granted herein are provided on a
    temporary basis and can be withdrawn by Interplay Productions at any time.
    All rights not expressly granted are reserved.

The same file opens by describing the SDK as "a bare-bones compilation of the
tools necessary to create user modifications to Kingpin", and Xatrix promoted it
at release as being for exactly that. Those two statements have never been
reconciled by the rights holders, and no permission to redistribute modified SDK
source or compiled game libraries has ever been granted in writing. None is
claimed here.

The gamesrc/ subtree of kpsdk.zip, which is what this repository was seeded
from, does not itself contain that readme — it sits one directory above.


2. id Software Quake II — attribution restored
-----------------------------------------------

Copyright (C) 1997-2001 Id Software, Inc.

Kingpin is built on Quake II, and much of the SDK is id's game source with
Kingpin code layered on top. Measured at commit 008a609 (2026-09-11) against
id's released Quake II game/ directory: 26 files here have an id counterpart,
and 13,498 lines — 16.1% of the source at that commit — are line-identical to
id's code.

None of those files carries id's copyright notice. Xatrix removed the notices in
1999, when they held a commercial engine licence from id and no obligation to
keep them. This section restores the attribution.

On 2001-12-21, after Kingpin shipped, id released the Quake II source including
the game/ directory under the GNU General Public License version 2. That release
is the place to obtain id's code under free terms:

    https://github.com/id-Software/Quake-2

It does not place this repository, or Xatrix's Kingpin code, under the GPL. The
id-derived lines here arrived via Xatrix's 1999 SDK under section 1's terms, not
via id's 2001 GPL release.


3. NavLib reconstruction — MIT
-------------------------------

Copyright (c) 2026 FREDZ

external/navlib/ is a clean reconstruction of the SDK's binary-only NavLib.lib,
licensed MIT. Its full licence text is at external/navlib/LICENSE and must be
retained. Upstream: https://github.com/drFredz/Kingpin_NavLib


4. Modifications and build system — MIT
----------------------------------------

Copyright (c) 2026 moly

This section covers only the parts of this repository that are the repository
owner's own work, namely:

  - the build system and documentation — everything in this repository that is
    not SDK source or vendored third-party code
  - the changes made to the SDK sources in src/, as recorded in this
    repository's git history

It does not, and cannot, cover the SDK code those changes were made to.

